# Byte-exact test fixtures must check out with LF endings on every platform.
# Windows runners default to CRLF conversion, which inserts a byte per line
# and shifts every RawSpan offset — breaking the Loader's byte-slice span
# assertions (which is precisely what they exist to verify). See the Windows
# CI failure fixed alongside this file: startOffset 40 vs 39, size 348 vs 347.
*.arxml text eol=lf
